---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { u, getManifest } from '../lib/data.mjs';

const REPO_ISSUES = 'https://github.com/alexchouck-hash/modafied/issues';
const manifest = getManifest();

// The dispute log. Empty is a fact worth printing rather than a section worth hiding: it means
// nobody has challenged a card yet, not that challenges are unwelcome (CLAUDE.md I4).
const DISPUTES = [];
---

<Layout title="Disputes">
  <div style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 2.25rem; font-weight: 800; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">Disputes</h1>
    <p style="font-size: 1.1rem; color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 820px;">
      If a card is wrong about your feed, the fix is a public dispute with a reproduction attached, and the
      resolution is a written decision or an experiment. Nothing here gets fixed by a quiet edit, including when the
      quiet edit would be in your favour.
    </p>
  </div>

  <section style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-left: 5px solid var(--primary-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-subtle); margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.15rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">What a dispute has to contain</h2>
    <p style="margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
      A reproduction. Not an opinion about the result, but the inputs and the command that produced a different one.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
      This is not a hurdle for its own sake. A score here is a function of an archive and a code version, so a
      disagreement is either a bug in the code, a bug in the catalog entry, or a disagreement about the method. All
      three are answerable, and all three are answered differently. Without a reproduction, nobody can tell which
      one you have found.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">How to file one</h2>
    <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1rem;">
      <div style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.1rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700;">1. Pin what you are disputing</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.35rem;">
          The source id, the dimension or the accuracy figure, the <code>method_version</code> on the card, and the
          <code>generated_at</code> stamp. A card is only meaningful with its version, because the method moves and
          old cards keep the version that produced them.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.1rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700;">2. Recompute it</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.35rem;">
          From the published archive, at the same timestamp, and show what you got. The recomputation is what makes
          the dispute actionable.
        </p>
        <pre>{`make reproduce SOURCE=<id> AS_OF=<timestamp>`}</pre>
        <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #78350f; background: #fffbeb; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem;">
          The verifier this command lives in is not published yet, so today an outside party cannot run it. Until it
          is, file the dispute anyway with the artifacts you can reach and say what you expected instead; the
          missing verifier is our problem, not yours. Progress on it is on the <a href={u('/replicas')}>replication page</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div style="border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.1rem;">
        <h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700;">3. Open a public issue</h3>
        <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-muted); margin-top: 0.35rem;">
          <a href={REPO_ISSUES}>On the repository</a>, titled with the source id. It gets a public answer and it is
          listed on this page, whichever way it goes.
        </p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: #78350f; background: #fffbeb; border-radius: 4px; padding: 0.5rem 0.7rem; margin-top: 0.5rem;">
          That repository is private today, so the link works for us and not for you. The same companion public
          repository that carries the verifier is where issues and catalog pull requests will live, and until it
          ships neither disputes nor submissions have the public front door this site describes. Saying so is more
          use to you than a link that returns a 404.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">How it is resolved</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th style="width: 15rem;">What you found</th><th>What happens</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>A bug in the scoring code</strong></td>
          <td>Fixed, with a golden fixture added so it cannot come back silently. Affected cards recompute on the next publish. The fix and the fixture are both public.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>A wrong catalog entry</strong></td>
          <td>Corrected by a pull request against <code>catalog/sources/&lt;id&gt;.yaml</code>. If your feed is described wrongly, this is usually the answer, and you can send the correction yourself.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>A disagreement with the method</strong></td>
          <td>An ADR, argued in public, or an experiment that settles it with data. If it changes the method it changes it for every source at once, with a version bump and 30 days of both versions side by side.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><strong>The card is right and you dislike it</strong></td>
          <td>It stands, and the dispute stays listed with that answer. This is the case the process exists for.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); font-size: 0.9rem; max-width: 820px;">
      What never happens: a score adjusted by hand, a card pulled to end an argument, or a method changed for one
      source. There is no override switch to reach for, which is the point of not having built one.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section style="margin-bottom: 3rem;">
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 1rem;">The log</h2>
    {DISPUTES.length === 0 ? (
      <div style="border: 1px dashed var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; background: var(--bg-subtle);">
        <p style="font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">No disputes have been filed.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 0.92rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
          Five sources are scored, the first cards published recently, and nobody has challenged one yet. Read that
          as a young benchmark rather than a vindicated one. Every dispute that is filed appears here, including the
          ones we lose.
        </p>
      </div>
    ) : (
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Filed</th><th>Source</th><th>Claim</th><th>Resolution</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {DISPUTES.map((d) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{d.filed}</td>
              <td><a href={u(`/scorecards/${d.source_id}`)}>{d.source_id}</a></td>
              <td>{d.claim}</td>
              <td>{d.resolution}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    )}
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2 style="font-size: 1.5rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">What you are disputing against</h2>
    <p style="color: var(--text-muted); max-width: 820px; margin-bottom: 0.75rem;">
      Every artifact behind a card is listed with its sha256 in the manifest. Pin it, and a dispute can name exactly
      which bytes it disagrees with.
    </p>
    <pre>{`curl -s https://modafied.org/v1/manifest.json | sha256sum`}</pre>
    {manifest.generated_at && (
      <p style="font-size: 0.85rem; color: var(--text-muted);">
        Manifest currently published at {manifest.generated_at}, covering {manifest.files?.length ?? 0} artifacts.
      </p>
    )}
  </section>
</Layout>
